+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08 and covered two capabilities at once: changing a booked visit and cancelling one. That ADR set the terms for any later move. Narrowing the row is a recorded owner decision carrying its own non-goal ADR, and a request never reopens the row by implication.
+
+The owner made that decision on 2026-08-28. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is wanted; cancellation is not.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner has asked for the correction flow, so the row no longer describes the intended boundary.
+2. **Drop NG-5 entirely.** Allow correction and cancellation together. Rejected: cancelling withdraws a booked visit, which is the lifecycle state the sample deliberately carries nowhere. NG-4 keeps deletion out for the same reason.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen). Correction joins the owner and pet update flows the sample already demonstrates.
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is a requirement, recorded as REQ-VIS-003. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope under a narrowed NG-5.
+
+The sample now corrects every record forward — owner, pet, and visit alike — and still withdraws nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Forward-only correction becomes the sample's uniform pattern across all three record kinds.
+- NG-4 is untouched. Deleting an owner, a pet, or a visit stays out.
+- The correction surface carries no visible entry point in this round. That boundary is deliberate and recorded against REQ-VIS-003, not an oversight.
+- Narrowing NG-4, or narrowing NG-5 further, remains a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the amended preamble.
+- [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction capability this narrowing admits.
+- [ADR: Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — amended in part by this decision.
